x['title']='The toroidal spectral strategy for the Riemann hypothesis'
x['statement']=r'The recognizable strategy seeks a spectral realization of the toroidal automorphic space that forces the relevant Eisenstein parameters onto the critical line. The necessary conclusion is temperedness of the relevant constituents; unitarity alone allows complementary-series representations and is insufficient. One must specify the topology, invariant pairing, spectral identification and exclusion of non-tempered constituents. Formal invariance under the Laplacian proves none of these requirements.'
x['fate']=r'\citet[final sections]{zagier1981eisenstein} gives the earlier strategy and its difficulties. \citet[Introduction and main results]{cornelissenlorscheid2011toroidal} identifies the toroidal spectrum and explicitly states the RH connection in terms of temperedness. It does not prove that needed restriction. \citet{clay2026riemann} confirms that RH remains open.'
x['literal_correctness']='false as written'
x['publication_match']='partial'
x['present_status']=r'As of 12 November 2026, the algebraic toroidal spectrum is substantially understood, but the required critical-line spectral restriction is unproved. The notebook\textquoteright s unqualified appeal to unitarity does not establish RH.'
correction('P001342-P001343','toroidal spectral criterion','unitarity of the representation would imply RH','The relevant spectral conclusion is temperedness; unitarity alone includes complementary series.','Cornelissen-Lorscheid Introduction states the RH strategy with tempered constituents; the positive pairing alone is not enough.')
next(x for x in items if x['id']=='1986-708.6')['verification']='indirect'
x=next(x for x in items if x['id']=='1986-712.15')
x['class']='E'
x['fate']=r'\citet[Introduction, p.~217, and Theorem~5.2, p.~237]{suslin1991bloch} is the precise later publication: Russian original 1990, English issue 1991 (translation copyright 1992). Suslin explicitly says that most results of the paper were obtained in 1982. The April 1987 notebook independently witnesses the prepublication circulation of the Bloch--K-theory connection. It is therefore treated as exposition of an already circulating result, while the introduction does not date every refinement of the final theorem separately. The theorem was read directly and specifies an infinite field, the indecomposable quotient and the modified roots-of-unity torsion term.'
x['reconstruction']=r'The rational comparison is stated without the convention-sensitive integral extension. The classification records prior circulation, rather than inferring a post-1987 discovery from the printed date.'
